Hey [~accountid:712020:9e34cd6d-2b7e-4426-8409-fbc13d3aa17a] Please find the GDoc version here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1soENZjJAc4--EzShPVwsK6ZuJLuKSdcQ76X1kpcjFrs/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1soENZjJAc4--EzShPVwsK6ZuJLuKSdcQ76X1kpcjFrs/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] 

Regarding the proposed changes:

{quote}Remove the penalty clauses from clause 2.6.{quote}

_I’m not exactly sure I understand what is meant by ‘penalty clauses’, but 2.6 is a necessary clause for us. It cannot be removed as it is a standard commercial safeguard designed to ensure that payments for services already rendered are made on time. This clause ensures that, in the event of late payment, we are entitled to interest and reasonable recovery costs — which is standard practice in B2B commercial agreements._

{quote}Clause '3.2' should be noted as '3.1'.{quote}

_Fixed._

{quote}In clause 3.2, the following should be stated: ‘This Agreement is concluded for a period of 1 year. If no notification of termination of the Agreement is received, it will be extended for the same period under the same conditions. The Agreement can be unilaterally terminated by either party with one month's prior written notice.'{quote}

_If it’s strictly demanded, fine, but it is much more restrictive than we have in our General Terms (GTC). Under Clause 7.1 of the GTC, the Agreement is open-ended and effective from the moment of sign-up until terminated by either party​. Additionally, Clause 7.2 allows either party to terminate the Agreement at any time with_ *_7 days’ prior notice_*_, ensuring flexibility._ 

{quote}Add clause 3.3: 'The Customer is released from liability for the untimely execution of orders, and the Contractor bears full financial responsibility for the damage caused to the Customer and those using the service due to the actions or inactions of the individuals with whom the Contractor cooperates.'{quote}

_We cannot accept this as it contradicts the core principle of our business model as an intermediary platform._

_The proposed clause is incompatible with Clause 6.3.6 of the GTCs, which clearly states that Bolt is_ *_not liable_* _for the actions, errors, or omissions of third parties providing services via the Bolt platform (e.g. drivers)​. These individuals are independent service providers, and_ *_we do not employ or control them_*_. Furthermore, under Clause 1.3, Bolt Services are defined as platform-based services, and Clause 3.7 clarifies that Bolt acts as a commercial agent on behalf of service providers,_ *_not as the service provider itself_*_​. Holding Bolt financially liable for their conduct would falsely imply an employment or principal liability relationship, which we explicitly disclaim._

{quote}Add clause 3.4: 'The Contractor must implement the necessary exchange system to confirm that the order was placed by the Customer. Otherwise, the Customer is released from liability for any resulting disagreements.'{quote}

_We cannot accept it since it conflicts with how Bolt Business is structured. Under Clause 2.3 of the GTCs, the Customer is responsible for managing access to the Business Portal, including adding and removing Users and setting their usage limits​. We provide all necessary administrative tools via the Business Portal to ensure that only authorized individuals place orders._

_Moreover, Clause 6.4 clearly states that the Customer is liable for all activities of its representatives and Users, including unauthorized or fraudulent usage​. Shifting this responsibility to us undermines the control mechanisms already placed in the Customer’s hands and opens the door to disputes over legitimate transactions._

_So, we provide the tools, but the Customer controls who can act on its behalf, and therefore cannot be released from liability due to their internal mismanagement._



Please feel free to ping me in case you have any further questions!

