🔴  *Problem →*  The total order counts often reflects finished trips, not those scenarios where orders were rejected including the fraud rejections that we normally still count as RDNH cases → fake orders/orders that did not occur

To define RDNH cases we currently detect: 

* {{additional.weekly.rejectedStrategyCount.DRIVER_DID_NOT_MOVE }}
* {{additional.weekly.rejectedStrategyCount.RIDE_TOO_SHORT_TIME  }}
* {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.RIDE_DID_NOT_HAPPEN  }}
* {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.DRIVER_DID_NOT_PICK_UP_RIDER  }}
* {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.GPS_UPFRONT}}  

The last three strategies from finished order flags could also be sufficient for this purpose as those orders ‘happened’ (?){color:#bf2600} [Needs confirmation]{color}

* {{additional.weekly.orderCount}} 

*_Mock Rule Concept DRIVER:_* 

:purple_star: {color:#403294}*AML_DRIVER_FAKE_RIDES* {color}:purple_star:

* {{additional.weekly.orderCount}} >= 10
*  {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.RIDE_DID_NOT_HAPPEN}} or {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.DRIVER_DID_NOT_PICK_UP_RIDER }} or {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.GPS_UPFRONT}}  / {{additional.weekly.orderCount}}  >= 0.5

*_Mock Rule Concept FLEET:_* 

:purple_star: {color:#403294}*AML_FLEET_FAKE_RIDES_MID* {color}:purple_star:

*  Med risk: {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.RIDE_DID_NOT_HAPPEN}} or {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.DRIVER_DID_NOT_PICK_UP_RIDER }} or {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.GPS_UPFRONT}}  / {{additional.weekly.orderCount}}  >= 0.05

:purple_star: {color:#403294}*AML_FLEET_FAKE_RIDES_HIGH* {color}:purple_star:

* High risk: 
** add minimum limit for {{additional.weekly.orderCount}}  to exclude odd scenarios 
** {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.RIDE_DID_NOT_HAPPEN}} or {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.DRIVER_DID_NOT_PICK_UP_RIDER }} or {{additional.weekly.strategyCount.GPS_UPFRONT}}  / {{additional.weekly.orderCount}}  >= 0.10

🔴  *Problem → do we count individually or together → if we count together we’d also need count unique order with relevant flags included (as otherwise we overcount)* 

