We have prepared ‘standard data protection clauses’ that can be included in LOE’s with external law firms below:

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*1. Data Protection*

1.1.  Each party acknowledges that it acts as an independent data controller in respect of any personal data it receives from the other party, or otherwise processes, in connection with the services and relationship governed by this Agreement. This includes any personal data relating to the other party’s personnel (such as names, contact details, roles, and other professional information), which is processed for the purposes of managing and administering the business relationship between the parties (“*Shared Personal Data*”).

1.2.  In respect of such Shared Personal Data, each party shall:

(a)    comply with all applicable data protection and privacy laws and regulations, including, where relevant, the General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (“*Applicable Data Protection Law*”);

(b)    only process the Shared Personal Data as necessary for the performance of this Agreement, to comply with legal obligations, or, where permitted by Applicable Data Protection Law, to send communications relating to its legal services, regulatory updates, or business operations;

(c)    implement and maintain appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect Shared Personal Data against accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorised disclosure or access;

(d)    ensure that any persons authorised to process the Shared Personal Data are subject to a duty of strict confidentiality; and

(e)    ensure that any transfer of Shared Personal Data to another country or territory outside the jurisdiction in which it was originally collected is carried out in accordance with Applicable Data Protection Law, including (where required) the implementation of appropriate safeguards.

1.3.      Each party shall, to the extent reasonably necessary, provide assistance to the other in responding to any data subject request, regulatory inquiry, or complaint relating to Shared Personal Data. Nothing in this clause shall be construed as creating joint responsibility, and each party remains solely responsible for its own compliance with Applicable Data Protection Law.

1.4.      Each party shall, to the extent permitted by law, notify the other party without undue delay if it becomes aware of a personal data breach affecting Shared Personal Data received from the other party under this Agreement. Where the other party is Bolt, notifications shall be sent to [privacy@bolt.eu|mailto:privacy@bolt.eu].

1.5.      Each party shall retain Shared Personal Data only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes of this Agreement or as required by applicable law, and shall take reasonable steps to securely delete or anonymise such data when no longer required.
{panel}

