ts own profile ID."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Certain categories of driver data (e.g., acceptance rate, average rating, order history, and online time) will be segregated according to driver profile. Other categories of data (name, profile picture, contact information, consents, account status, login history) will be synced across driver profiles and stored on a partner profile level."}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colwidth":[212],"background":"#ffffff"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"We need to have a functionality for extracting data on a driver profile level (not just on a partner profile level)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is because once Project Green is launched, it is foreseeable that a driver may submit a DSAR for their ‘agency model data’ or their ‘principal model data'. If we do not have a way of sourcing this efficiently, this will create a headache for us."}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colwidth":[327],"background":"#e3fcef"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I understand this is already being pushed forward (see "},{"type":"text","text":"here","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/6178701679/Couriers+and+driver+work+profiles+in+PDE#3.5-Use-distinct-DriverIds-and-CourierIds-in-Plugins-and-abstract-%E2%80%9Cprofiles%E2%80%9D-in-Admin-Panel-~-5MD"}},{"type":"underline"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":" "}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"mention","attrs":{"id":"641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d","accessLevel":"","localId":"6be97304-da58-4c08-a5e2-be885d9c07a2"}},{"type":"text","text":" DONE"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"These changes will be made soon for both drivers and couriers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":" "}]},{"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type"